  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "comment": "One liter of the modified GS-2 medium contained 1.5 g KH2PO4, 2.9 g K2HPO4, 3 g sodium citrate tribasic dihydrate (Na3C6H5O7), 2.1 g urea, 5 g 3-(N-morpholino) propanesulfonic acid (MOPS), 2 mg resazurin, and 1 g L-cysteine."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": "A 10-fold trace salt solution contained 26 mg MgCl2, 11.3 mg CaCl2, and 0.125 mg FeSO4.7H2O."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "A 100-fold vitamin solution contained 2 mg pyridoxine hydrochloride, 0.2 mg biotin, 0.4 mg p-aminobenzoic acid and 0.2 mg vitamin B12 [39]."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": "Trace salt and vitamin solutions were sterilized using a 0.22-µm filter (StarTech, Taiwan). All solutions were prepared with distilled water from an EcoQ Combo (LionBio, Taiwan)."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": "The pH of the GS-2 medium was adjusted to 7.2 using 5 M NaOH and purged extensively with pure nitrogen gas to create an anaerobic environment."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": "GS-2 medium was autoclaved at 121 °C for 20 min, and 1% (v/v) trace salt solution and 1% (v/v) vitamin solution were added to the modified GS-2 when the medium was cooled to 50 °C."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 11,
      "comment": ""
    }
  ]
}